                    <msContents>
                        <summary>A single copper plate found in a group of five copper plates of the Parijātavaneśvara temple of Tirukkaḷar, found altogether strung on a copper ring. Records a donation of land for the expenses of two officiating Brahmins. Time of Rājādhirāja I Cōḻa.</summary>
                    </msContents>
                    <physDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <p>
                                No distinction between <foreign>e</foreign> and <foreign>ē</foreign>,
                                nor between <foreign>o</foreign> and <foreign>ō</foreign>.
                                Medial <foreign>i</foreign> and <foreign>ī</foreign> interchangeable.
                                <foreign>n</foreign> and <foreign>ñ</foreign> interchangeable.
                            </p>
                        </handDesc>
                    </physDesc>
                </msDesc>
            </sourceDesc>
